('7f6902f1-b7c4-5f40-bd4f-dbfd89eab292','8b822a13-1f43-5f46-8722-31fd8d95602d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','not open',null,'keep your mouth shut','باز نیست',array['closed']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['tightly/tight shut He went on sobbing, his eyes tight shut.','firmly shut The door remained firmly shut.','something slams/bangs shut The front door slammed shut.','something swings shut The gate swung shut behind her.','pull/kick/slam something shut He pulled the trapdoor shut over his head.','keep something shut When it’s so hot, we keep the doors and windows shut and put on the air conditioner.','screw/squeeze your eyes shut (= shut your eyes tight )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Is the door shut properly?","translation":"آیا درب به درستی بسته شده است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000952992.mp3"},{"sentence":"She kept the windows shut , for fear of burglars.","translation":"او از ترس سارقان پنجره ها را بسته نگه داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001673531.mp3"},{"sentence":"He sat with his eyes shut .","translation":"با چشمان بسته نشست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000952993.mp3"},{"sentence":"The windows were tightly shut .","translation":"پنجره ها را محکم بسته بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001673540.mp3"},{"sentence":"The door slammed shut behind him.","translation":"در پشت سرش محکم بسته شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000952996.mp3"},{"sentence":"Jenny pulled the window shut.","translation":"جنی پنجره را بست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000952999.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('7861dc04-8317-5bb7-9a38-bf5967606b9c','8b822a13-1f43-5f46-8722-31fd8d95602d',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if a shop , bar etc is shut, it is not open for business',null,null,'اگر مغازه، بار و غیره بسته باشد، برای تجارت باز نیست',array['closed']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['tightly/tight shut He went on sobbing, his eyes tight shut.','firmly shut The door remained firmly shut.','something slams/bangs shut The front door slammed shut.','something swings shut The gate swung shut behind her.','pull/kick/slam something shut He pulled the trapdoor shut over his head.','keep something shut When it’s so hot, we keep the doors and windows shut and put on the air conditioner.','screw/squeeze your eyes shut (= shut your eyes tight )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"in the evening when the shops are shut","translation":"عصر که مغازه ها تعطیل هستند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000953006.mp3"},{"sentence":"Sorry, but we’re shut.","translation":"متاسفم، اما ما بسته ایم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001673548.mp3"},{"sentence":"The first four hotels we tried were shut for the winter.","translation":"چهار هتل اولی که امتحان کردیم برای زمستان تعطیل بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000953009.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('cd230ad7-9552-57c2-9df9-1fb382c74fea','1daf2bd1-81eb-5b76-a45d-e12ec8dc9413',1,'ill','بیمار','spoken & written','suffering from a disease or illness',null,null,'بیمار، مریض؛ حال‌بده (حالت)؛ آشفته (پرنده)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['get sick (= become ill ) The boy got sick, and he just got worse and worse.','fall/take sick formal (= become ill, especially with something serious or that will last a long time ) He fell sick and died within a matter of weeks.','be off sick British English , be out sick American English (= be away from work or school because you are ill ) Half my staff were off sick.','call/phone/ring in sick (= phone to say you are not coming in to work because you are ill ) I could have called in sick, but I knew you needed this report.','sick leave (= time that you can stay away from work because you are ill ) He returned to duty after two months’ sick leave.','sick pay (= money paid to an employee who is too ill to work ) Only full-time employees got sick pay.','somebody''s sick bed (= the bed where a sick person is lying ) He left his sick bed to play in the game.','the sick room (= the room where a sick person is ) She had spent the last hour in her mother’s sick room.','the sick bay (= a room where there are beds for people who are sick, for example on a ship or in a school ) I was confined to the ship''s sick bay until we arrived back in Liverpool.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"His mother’s very sick.","translation":"مادرش خیلی مریض است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000683100.mp3"},{"sentence":"Maria can’t come in today because she’s sick.","translation":"ماریا امروز نمی تواند وارد شود زیرا بیمار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001673150.mp3"},{"sentence":"a sick child","translation":"یک کودک بیمار","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000683101.mp3"},{"sentence":"a sick animal","translation":"یک حیوان بیمار","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001673151.mp3"},{"sentence":"I have been sick with flu.","translation":"من به آنفولانزا مبتلا شده ام.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001673154.mp3"},{"sentence":"At the last minute, I got sick and couldn’t go.","translation":"در آخرین لحظه مریض شدم و نتوانستم بروم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000683106.mp3"},{"sentence":"Two of his employees were out sick.","translation":"دو نفر از کارمندانش مریض بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001673164.mp3"},{"sentence":"I was off sick for four days with the flu.","translation":"من چهار روز با آنفولانزا مریض بودم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000683114.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was upset because it was the first day of the sale and Astrid had called in sick.","translation":"او ناراحت بود زیرا روز اول فروش بود و آسترید بیمار تماس گرفته بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001673168.mp3"},{"sentence":"What will happen to the business if you fall sick (= become ill ) or die?","translation":"اگر بیمار شوید (= مریض شوید) یا بمیرید، چه اتفاقی برای کسب و کار خواهد افتاد؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001673169.mp3"},{"sentence":"He took sick (= became ill ) and died a week later.","translation":"مریض شد (= بیمار شد) و یک هفته بعد درگذشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000683123.mp3"},{"sentence":"Pete’s at home in bed, as sick as a dog (= very sick ) .","translation":"پیت در خانه در رختخواب است، به اندازه یک سگ بیمار است (= بسیار بیمار).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00803.mp3"}]'::jsonb,12),
('9c48247a-319c-53a6-8dde-380baf686f3a','1daf2bd1-81eb-5b76-a45d-e12ec8dc9413',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be sick','بیمار، مریض؛ حال‌بده (حالت)؛ آشفته (پرنده)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['get sick (= become ill ) The boy got sick, and he just got worse and worse.','fall/take sick formal (= become ill, especially with something serious or that will last a long time ) He fell sick and died within a matter of weeks.','be off sick British English , be out sick American English (= be away from work or school because you are ill ) Half my staff were off sick.','call/phone/ring in sick (= phone to say you are not coming in to work because you are ill ) I could have called in sick, but I knew you needed this report.','sick leave (= time that you can stay away from work because you are ill ) He returned to duty after two months’ sick leave.','sick pay (= money paid to an employee who is too ill to work ) Only full-time employees got sick pay.','somebody''s sick bed (= the bed where a sick person is lying ) He left his sick bed to play in the game.','the sick room (= the room where a sick person is ) She had spent the last hour in her mother’s sick room.','the sick bay (= a room where there are beds for people who are sick, for example on a ship or in a school ) I was confined to the ship''s sick bay until we arrived back in Liverpool.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
