('11986318-3fed-54a2-842e-9dee4a4d85f1','893b1241-713f-5088-a2be-511ae6544659',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used when you see two things that are exactly the same',null,null,'زمانی استفاده می شود که دو چیز را دقیقاً مشابه می بینید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Hey, snap! My hat’s the same as yours.","translation":"هی، ضربه محکم و ناگهانی! کلاه من همون کلاه شماست","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000670487.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('544b3107-8e0d-5959-8e99-2ed7a4aa30ad','893b1241-713f-5088-a2be-511ae6544659',2,null,null,'spoken & written','said in the game of snap when two cards that are the same are put down',null,null,'در بازی اسنپ زمانی گفته می شود که دو کارت یکسان کنار گذاشته شوند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('689ee687-71bc-5539-8884-5f6de1eab3de','c0f58aff-d0a1-5c1a-ae1c-9b4d065487d3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','soft white pieces of frozen water that fall from the sky in cold weather and cover the ground','[ uncountable ]',null,'برف، برف (سنگین)؛ برف (ساعت)؛ برف (مصنوعی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['snow falls Outside in the dark, snow was falling silently.','snow settles (= stays on the ground ) The snow was beginning to settle.','snow drifts (= is blown into deep piles ) The snow had drifted up against the hedge.','snow covers/blankets something The ground was covered with snow.','snow melts (= turns to water ) The snow has melted and the ground is bare once more.','deep The snow was quite deep in places.','heavy (= when a lot of snow falls ) France has been expecting heavy snow all week.','fresh I had watched the tracks I’d made disappear under fresh snow.','powdery The powdery snow flies up as I walk through it.','wet snow He cleared the wet snow from the car windscreen.','light snow (= when only a small amount falls ) A light snow had begun to fall.','driving snow (= falling fast ) We walked home through driving snow.','swirling snow (= blowing around as it falls ) It was difficult to see in the swirling snow.','several inches/feet of snow More than eight inches of snow fell in 48 hours.','a blanket/carpet of snow Within an hour, Bucharest was buried under a blanket of snow.','flakes of snow (= individual pieces of snow ) A few flakes of snow started to fall.','a flurry of snow/a snow flurry (= when a small amount of snow blows around in the wind ) The day was cold, with a few flurries of snow.','a fall of snow (= an occasion when it snows ) We had our first fall of snow in mid-November.','a drift of snow (= snow blown into a pile by the wind ) Sheep became buried in six-foot drifts of snow.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Snow was falling heavily as we entered the village.","translation":"وقتی وارد روستا شدیم برف شدیدی می بارید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001780100.mp3"},{"sentence":"I could see footprints in the snow.","translation":"می توانستم رد پا را در برف ببینم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001780105.mp3"},{"sentence":"The town was buried under three feet of snow.","translation":"شهر زیر سه فوت برف مدفون شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001624954.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('fc8f012f-b5ea-5d66-9518-baf9ac10533d','c0f58aff-d0a1-5c1a-ae1c-9b4d065487d3',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a period of time in which snow falls','[ countable ]',null,'دوره زمانی که در آن برف می بارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['snow falls Outside in the dark, snow was falling silently.','snow settles (= stays on the ground ) The snow was beginning to settle.','snow drifts (= is blown into deep piles ) The snow had drifted up against the hedge.','snow covers/blankets something The ground was covered with snow.','snow melts (= turns to water ) The snow has melted and the ground is bare once more.','deep The snow was quite deep in places.','heavy (= when a lot of snow falls ) France has been expecting heavy snow all week.','fresh I had watched the tracks I’d made disappear under fresh snow.','powdery The powdery snow flies up as I walk through it.','wet snow He cleared the wet snow from the car windscreen.','light snow (= when only a small amount falls ) A light snow had begun to fall.','driving snow (= falling fast ) We walked home through driving snow.','swirling snow (= blowing around as it falls ) It was difficult to see in the swirling snow.','several inches/feet of snow More than eight inches of snow fell in 48 hours.','a blanket/carpet of snow Within an hour, Bucharest was buried under a blanket of snow.','flakes of snow (= individual pieces of snow ) A few flakes of snow started to fall.','a flurry of snow/a snow flurry (= when a small amount of snow blows around in the wind ) The day was cold, with a few flurries of snow.','a fall of snow (= an occasion when it snows ) We had our first fall of snow in mid-November.','a drift of snow (= snow blown into a pile by the wind ) Sheep became buried in six-foot drifts of snow.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"one of the heaviest snows this winter","translation":"یکی از سنگین ترین برف های زمستان امسال","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000671744.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
