('e5060250-cf71-555c-8dab-70a5d8cd648c','766a3a9a-0c62-5682-8769-a6f561a96d9b',1,'movement','حرکت','spoken & written','the movement you make when you put one foot in front of or behind the other when walking','[ countable ]',null,'قدم، گام؛ قدم (قدم زدن)؛ پله (کوتاه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a video of baby’s first steps","translation":"ویدئویی از اولین قدم های کودک","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636063.mp3"},{"sentence":"He took one step and fell.","translation":"یک قدم برداشت و افتاد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636064.mp3"},{"sentence":"Tom took a step back and held the door open.","translation":"تام قدمی عقب رفت و در را باز نگه داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636072.mp3"},{"sentence":"I had to retrace my steps (= go back the way I came ) several times before I found the shop.","translation":"قبل از اینکه مغازه را پیدا کنم مجبور شدم چندین بار قدم هایم را برگردم (= از راهی که آمده ام به عقب برگردم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636073.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('1e193ddc-5312-5fa5-a291-98be4a7cfd01','766a3a9a-0c62-5682-8769-a6f561a96d9b',2,'action','اقدام','spoken & written','one of a series of things that you do in order to deal with a problem or to succeed','[ countable ]',null,'یکی از مجموعه کارهایی که برای مقابله با مشکل یا موفقیت انجام می دهید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['take a step The authority will take steps to reunite the child and his family.','an important/major/big step The move is seen as a major step forward for UK firms.','the first step The first step in resolving conflict is to understand what the other person wants.','the next step He met in Washington with his campaign advisers to plan his next step.','a small step This is a small step in the right direction.','a positive step (= an action that will have a good effect ) This is a positive step which gives cause for some optimism.','an unusual/unprecedented step (= something that is not usually done/has never been done before ) Police last night took the unusual step of releasing photographs of him.','a drastic step The government is wary of taking any drastic steps that would scare off foreign investment.','a bold step We welcome the bold step taken by President Bush.','a tentative step (= a small action, which is not done in a very determined way ) The Institute has taken a tentative step towards opening up its meetings to the public.','a logical step She felt she had an aptitude for medicine. Her next logical step would be to begin studying when the summer was over.','immediate steps We believe immediate steps could be taken to generate jobs.','reasonable steps They must take reasonable steps to ensure that this information is available to those who might benefit.','necessary steps We must be sure that we are taking the necessary steps to prevent the problem from getting a foothold here.','a step forward (= an action that makes things better ) The declaration which we have just signed is a big step forward for both of our nations.','a step backwards/a backward step (= an action that makes things worse ) A rationing system would be a major step backwards.','a step in the right direction (= an action that helps to improve things ) Environmentalists said the law was a step in the right direction.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"This is the first step in reforming the welfare system.","translation":"این اولین گام در اصلاح نظام رفاهی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000643933.mp3"},{"sentence":"The president took immediate steps to stop the fighting.","translation":"رئیس جمهور اقدامات فوری برای توقف درگیری انجام داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000643940.mp3"},{"sentence":"an important step towards peace","translation":"گامی مهم به سوی صلح","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000643936.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('371c65cd-886a-556c-8b96-4cb4f579038a','766a3a9a-0c62-5682-8769-a6f561a96d9b',3,'in a process','در یک فرآیند','spoken & written','a stage in a process, or a position on a scale','[ countable ]',null,'یک مرحله در یک فرآیند، یا یک موقعیت در یک مقیاس','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Each book goes up one step in difficulty.","translation":"هر کتاب در سختی یک پله بالا می رود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000643971.mp3"},{"sentence":"Record your result, and go on to step 3.","translation":"نتیجه خود را ثبت کنید و به مرحله 3 بروید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636100.mp3"},{"sentence":"the next step in the process","translation":"مرحله بعدی در روند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001780010.mp3"},{"sentence":"Drug companies influence the scientific process every step of the way (= during every stage ) .","translation":"شرکت های دارویی در هر مرحله (= در هر مرحله) بر فرآیند علمی تأثیر می گذارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000643975.mp3"},{"sentence":"Describe step by step (= describing each stage ) how you went about achieving your goal.","translation":"گام به گام (= توصیف هر مرحله) توضیح دهید که چگونه برای رسیدن به هدف خود پیش رفتید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636105.mp3"},{"sentence":"Moving to Cottage Grove represented a definite step up (= something that is better than you had before ) for my parents.","translation":"نقل مکان به کلبه گروو نشان دهنده یک گام قطعی (= چیزی که بهتر از قبل است) برای والدین من بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636110.mp3"},{"sentence":"He saw the job as a step down (= something that is worse than he had before ) .","translation":"او کار را به عنوان یک پله (= چیزی که بدتر از قبل است) دید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636117.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('451576cf-2811-5fcb-82ba-ab5c6e5ca52f','766a3a9a-0c62-5682-8769-a6f561a96d9b',4,'stair','پله','spoken & written','a flat narrow piece of wood or stone , especially one in a series, that you put your foot on when you are going up or down, especially outside a building','[ countable ]','doorstep 1 ( 1 )','یک تکه چوب یا سنگ مسطح باریک، مخصوصاً یکی در یک سری، که هنگام بالا یا پایین رفتن، به ویژه در خارج از ساختمان، پای خود را روی آن می گذارید.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Jenny sat on the step in front of the house, waiting.","translation":"جنی روی پله جلوی خانه نشست و منتظر بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000643956.mp3"},{"sentence":"He climbed the wooden steps and rang the bell.","translation":"از پله های چوبی بالا رفت و زنگ را به صدا درآورد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636122.mp3"},{"sentence":"a flight of (= set of ) broad stone steps","translation":"پرواز (= مجموعه ای از) پله های سنگی پهن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636128.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
