('7f84534a-1bf3-5121-a748-f2158e54bf4e','ac157f5f-3ae2-59aa-bf56-408db1e83069',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a story about exciting imaginary events',null,null,'حکایت، افسانه؛ حکایت (فرد)؛ حکایت (کار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a fairy tale It looked like a castle in a fairy tale.','a folk tale (= a traditional story ) a book of Scottish folk tales','a cautionary tale (= one that is told to warn someone about the dangers of something ) This cautionary tale illustrates the dangers of looking for quick profits.','a tall tale (= one that is difficult to believe and unlikely to be true ) She enjoyed making up tall tales to tell the children.','tell a tale He liked telling tales of his adventures in the wilderness.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"tales of adventure","translation":"داستان های ماجراجویی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001580272.mp3"},{"sentence":"a book of old Japanese folk tales (= traditional stories )","translation":"کتاب داستان های عامیانه قدیمی ژاپنی (= داستان های سنتی)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001827602.mp3"},{"sentence":"a fairy tale by Hans Christian Andersen","translation":"داستانی از هانس کریستین اندرسن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001990475.mp3"},{"sentence":"a cautionary tale (= one that is told to warn people about the dangers of something )","translation":"حکایت هشدار دهنده (= داستانی که برای هشدار دادن به مردم در مورد خطرات چیزی گفته می شود)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001990480.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('4ce3a292-b65b-5949-96d9-56d98d8c57bb','ac157f5f-3ae2-59aa-bf56-408db1e83069',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a description of interesting or exciting things that happened to someone, often one which is not completely true about every detail',null,null,'توصیفی از چیزهای جالب یا هیجان انگیزی که برای کسی اتفاق افتاده است، که اغلب در مورد تمام جزئیات کاملاً صادق نیست','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a fairy tale It looked like a castle in a fairy tale.','a folk tale (= a traditional story ) a book of Scottish folk tales','a cautionary tale (= one that is told to warn someone about the dangers of something ) This cautionary tale illustrates the dangers of looking for quick profits.','a tall tale (= one that is difficult to believe and unlikely to be true ) She enjoyed making up tall tales to tell the children.','tell a tale He liked telling tales of his adventures in the wilderness.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"tales of her life in post-war Berlin","translation":"داستان های زندگی او در برلین پس از جنگ","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000613856.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was in the middle of telling me a long tale about how he once met Bob Dylan.","translation":"او در میانه داستانی طولانی درباره نحوه ملاقات باب دیلن برای من تعریف می کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00873.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
