('64d2dc0e-5ee6-53d1-badc-246895817d29','9701444b-9d93-5cfc-b50e-ee37a313ca1e',3,'word','کلمه','spoken & written','a word or expression with a particular meaning, especially one that is used for a specific subject or type of language','[ countable ]','a contradiction in terms','کلمه یا عبارتی با معنای خاص، به ویژه معنایی که برای موضوع یا نوع خاصی از زبان به کار می رود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a legal/medical term The site provides a glossary of legal terms.','a technical term ‘Gender’ is a technical term in grammar.','a slang term ‘The Old Bill’ is a slang term for the police.','a derogatory/pejorative term (= one that is insulting or disapproving ) ‘Pinko’ is a derogatory term for someone with socialist ideas.','use a term a term used by psychiatrists','coin a term (= invent it ) Funk coined the term ‘vitamin’ in 1912.','a term of abuse (= a word that is offensive or deliberately rude ) ‘Geek’ is used as a term of abuse.','a term of endearment (= a word that expresses your love for someone ) terms of endearment like ‘love’, ‘dear’, and ‘honey’','in strong terms The pope condemned both Nazism and Communism in strong terms.','in glowing terms (= praising someone or something highly ) Friends and relatives speak of him in glowing terms.','in layman’s terms (= using ordinary words, not technical words ) Can you explain to me in layman’s terms how my computer works?']::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘Multimedia’ is the term for any technique combining sounds and images.","translation":"\"چند رسانه ای\" اصطلاحی برای هر تکنیکی است که صداها و تصاویر را ترکیب می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001801093.mp3"},{"sentence":"Journalists were told in no uncertain terms that they were not welcome.","translation":"به روزنامه‌نگاران به طور مشخص گفته شد که از آنها استقبال نمی‌شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001801127.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8ef09ebf-d4be-548c-893f-af163f6a1863','9701444b-9d93-5cfc-b50e-ee37a313ca1e',4,'period of time','دوره زمانی','spoken & written','a fixed period of time during which someone does something or something happens','[ countable ]','fixed-term','یک دوره زمانی ثابت که در طی آن کسی کاری انجام می دهد یا اتفاقی می افتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The mayor was coming to the end of his term in office.","translation":"شهردار به پایان دوره مسئولیت خود نزدیک می شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001589.mp3"},{"sentence":"the maximum term of imprisonment","translation":"حداکثر مدت حبس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001801140.mp3"},{"sentence":"The lease runs for a term of 99 years.","translation":"مدت اجاره به مدت 99 سال است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001801141.mp3"},{"sentence":"The men each received a 30-year prison term.","translation":"این افراد هر کدام به 30 سال زندان محکوم شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001801144.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('3ad4b5fc-f601-5624-b1c3-fe25eb7222aa','9701444b-9d93-5cfc-b50e-ee37a313ca1e',5,'school/university','مدرسه/دانشگاه','spoken & written','one of the periods of time that the school or university year is divided into. In Britain, there are usually three terms in a year.','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'یکی از دوره های زمانی که سال تحصیلی یا دانشگاهی به آن تقسیم می شود. در بریتانیا معمولاً سه ترم در سال وجود دارد.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The exams are at the end of the summer term.","translation":"امتحانات در پایان ترم تابستان است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000591064.mp3"},{"sentence":"Teachers often feel overworked in term time (= during the term ) .","translation":"معلمان اغلب در زمان ترم (= در طول ترم) احساس کار بیش از حد می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000591068.mp3"},{"sentence":"that all-important first day of term","translation":"اولین روز مهم ترم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001801159.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
