('a9cef164-dc45-5dcd-9b8f-a1b6df38aa36','55bf5055-095f-5fa6-bc1f-30a4f237668a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to try to make something happen by thinking about it very hard','[ transitive ]',null,'سعی کنید با فکر کردن به آن چیزی اتفاق بیفتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She was willing herself not to cry.","translation":"او حاضر بود گریه نکند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000487859.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('27acf25d-b1f6-5be7-9842-339a7fbb5d9b','55bf5055-095f-5fa6-bc1f-30a4f237668a',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to officially give something that you own to someone else after you die','[ transitive + to ]',null,'رسماً چیزی را که مالک آن هستید پس از مرگ به شخص دیگری بدهید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('16601e23-1b3d-5b6b-99d5-c3fa36447cb8','55bf5055-095f-5fa6-bc1f-30a4f237668a',3,null,null,'old use','to want something to happen','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'خواستن اتفاقی بیفتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The King wills it.","translation":"پادشاه اراده می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000487870.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('749dbcca-6009-5eb9-b2ad-7a95ca022c3b','09d32751-6564-5406-a85b-15436fdae944',1,'air','هوا','spoken & written','moving air, especially when it moves strongly or quickly in a current','[ countable, uncountable ]','crosswind , downwind , headwind , tailwind , trade wind , upwind','باد، باد (هوا)؛ باد (طبل)؛ باد (خون)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strong The wind was so strong he could hardly stand.','light/gentle (= not strong ) Winds tomorrow will be light.','high winds (= strong wind ) High winds are making driving conditions difficult.','a cold/chill wind There was a cold wind this afternoon.','an icy/biting/bitter wind (= very cold ) She shivered in the icy wind.','a gusty/blustery wind (= not blowing steadily ) A blustery wind was sending light flurries of rain against the window.','a fresh wind British English (= quite cold and strong ) It will feel colder in places exposed to a fresh northeasterly wind.','a 20-/40-mile-an-hour wind The walkers struggled in 35-mile-an-hour winds.','gale force/hurricane force winds (= very strong ) He was buffeted by the gale force winds.','the north/south etc wind (= coming from the north etc ) They sought shelter from the north wind.','a northerly/southerly etc wind (= coming from the north etc ) A fresh northerly wind was speeding the ship southwards.','the prevailing wind (= the most frequent wind in an area ) The prevailing wind comes from the west.','the wind blows A cold wind was blowing.','the wind picks up ( also the wind gets up British English ) (= becomes stronger ) The rain beat down and the wind was picking up.','the wind drops/dies down (= becomes less strong ) The wind had dropped a little.','the wind howls (= makes a lot of noise ) The wind howled round the house all night.','the wind changes (= starts blowing from a different direction ) The wind had to change before his fighting ships could sail against the Spanish.','a gust of wind A gust of wind rattled the window.','be blowing/swaying/flapping etc in the wind The trees were all swaying in the wind.','wind speed Wind speeds of up to 80 miles an hour were recorded.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The wind blew from the northeast.","translation":"باد از سمت شمال شرقی می وزد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001740677.mp3"},{"sentence":"Planes were unable to take off because of high winds.","translation":"هواپیماها به دلیل بادهای شدید قادر به بلند شدن نبودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001751.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('a2dd5ea8-99d6-533c-86fb-04c1718122b6','09d32751-6564-5406-a85b-15436fdae944',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'get/have wind of something','باد، باد (هوا)؛ باد (طبل)؛ باد (خون)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strong The wind was so strong he could hardly stand.','light/gentle (= not strong ) Winds tomorrow will be light.','high winds (= strong wind ) High winds are making driving conditions difficult.','a cold/chill wind There was a cold wind this afternoon.','an icy/biting/bitter wind (= very cold ) She shivered in the icy wind.','a gusty/blustery wind (= not blowing steadily ) A blustery wind was sending light flurries of rain against the window.','a fresh wind British English (= quite cold and strong ) It will feel colder in places exposed to a fresh northeasterly wind.','a 20-/40-mile-an-hour wind The walkers struggled in 35-mile-an-hour winds.','gale force/hurricane force winds (= very strong ) He was buffeted by the gale force winds.','the north/south etc wind (= coming from the north etc ) They sought shelter from the north wind.','a northerly/southerly etc wind (= coming from the north etc ) A fresh northerly wind was speeding the ship southwards.','the prevailing wind (= the most frequent wind in an area ) The prevailing wind comes from the west.','the wind blows A cold wind was blowing.','the wind picks up ( also the wind gets up British English ) (= becomes stronger ) The rain beat down and the wind was picking up.','the wind drops/dies down (= becomes less strong ) The wind had dropped a little.','the wind howls (= makes a lot of noise ) The wind howled round the house all night.','the wind changes (= starts blowing from a different direction ) The wind had to change before his fighting ships could sail against the Spanish.','a gust of wind A gust of wind rattled the window.','be blowing/swaying/flapping etc in the wind The trees were all swaying in the wind.','wind speed Wind speeds of up to 80 miles an hour were recorded.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
