('a6732e44-fc16-5f15-9b7d-795ffbd678e5','fce0723f-cd5e-5930-a01f-2468ff3e91b5',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a desire to do something, to have something, or to have something happen',null,'death wish','آرزو، حسرت؛ آرزو (قلبی)؛ آرزو (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a wish (= silently ask for something that you want to happen ) He blew out the candles and made a wish.','get/have your wish (= get what you want ) She wanted him to leave, and she got her wish.','grant/fulfil somebody''s wish (= give someone what they want ) His parents would now be able to grant his wish.','express a wish He expressed a wish to go to the United States.','respect somebody’s wishes (= do what someone wants ) We have to respect his wishes.','ignore somebody’s wishes It is important not to ignore the wishes of the patient.','somebody''s wish comes true His wish came true when he was called up to play for England.','somebody’s greatest/deepest wish ( also somebody’s dearest wish British English ) (= what they want most of all ) Her greatest wish was to see her parents again.','somebody’s last/final/dying wish Her last wish was to be buried in her husband’s grave.','a fervent wish (= a strong wish ) To die for Ireland was the fervent wish of every true patriot.','contrary to somebody''s wishes (= against what someone has said they want ) Contrary to her parents'' wishes, she decided not to go to university.','in accordance with somebody''s wishes formal (= following what someone wants ) In accordance with his wishes, he was buried next to his first wife.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"It’s important to listen to the wishes of the patient.","translation":"گوش دادن به خواسته های بیمار مهم است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001755.mp3"},{"sentence":"Despite her wish to continue working, she was forced to retire at the age of 62.","translation":"علیرغم تمایلش به ادامه کار، در سن 62 سالگی مجبور به بازنشستگی شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626567.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('3d8b3ee7-2050-5424-b0de-94eb05999ab4','fce0723f-cd5e-5930-a01f-2468ff3e91b5',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a silent request for something to happen as if by magic',null,null,'درخواستی بی سر و صدا برای اینکه چیزی اتفاق بیفتد، گویی از روی سحر و جادو','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a wish (= silently ask for something that you want to happen ) He blew out the candles and made a wish.','get/have your wish (= get what you want ) She wanted him to leave, and she got her wish.','grant/fulfil somebody''s wish (= give someone what they want ) His parents would now be able to grant his wish.','express a wish He expressed a wish to go to the United States.','respect somebody’s wishes (= do what someone wants ) We have to respect his wishes.','ignore somebody’s wishes It is important not to ignore the wishes of the patient.','somebody''s wish comes true His wish came true when he was called up to play for England.','somebody’s greatest/deepest wish ( also somebody’s dearest wish British English ) (= what they want most of all ) Her greatest wish was to see her parents again.','somebody’s last/final/dying wish Her last wish was to be buried in her husband’s grave.','a fervent wish (= a strong wish ) To die for Ireland was the fervent wish of every true patriot.','contrary to somebody''s wishes (= against what someone has said they want ) Contrary to her parents'' wishes, she decided not to go to university.','in accordance with somebody''s wishes formal (= following what someone wants ) In accordance with his wishes, he was buried next to his first wife.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Close your eyes and make a wish .","translation":"چشمانت را ببند و آرزو کن.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000493731.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
