('168eb04f-38fd-5d29-b75e-41ea635c2337','494ec3b8-55e7-565b-b992-2549c4de1b11',14,'news/information','اخبار/اطلاعات','old-fashioned','a piece of news or a message','[ singular, uncountable ]',null,'یک خبر یا یک پیام','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a new word Computer technology has brought many new words into our language.','the right/exact word (= the word that has the meaning you want ) He struggled to find the right word.','a German/Italian etc word Prosciutto is the Italian word for ham.','a long word She didn’t understand all the long words.','a short word a short word beginning with ‘d’ and ending with ‘g’','big words (= words that sound very important or serious ) It scares me, when you use big words like that.','a five-letter/nine-letter etc word Can you think of a six-letter word meaning ‘difficult’?','a rude word Someone had written a rude word on the back of his chair.','a swear word He learned a few swear words on the playground.','a dirty word (= a rude word ) You couldn’t say dirty words on television.','a four-letter word (= a very rude word ) The programme was full of four letter words.','a taboo word (= one that people are not allowed to use ) This has now become a taboo word.','say/speak a word She said the words ‘my husband’ in a firm voice.','use a word Be very careful how you use the word ‘natural’.','pronounce a word How do you pronounce this word?','spell a word I always find that word hard to spell.','have a word It is not true that Eskimos have more than forty words for snow.','find the word (= succeed in thinking of the right word to use ) She couldn’t find the words to explain how she felt.','search for words (= try to think of words to use ) She hesitated, searching for words.','look up a word (= try to find it in a book ) I looked the word up in my dictionary.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Word came that our duties would be changed.","translation":"خبر رسید که وظایف ما تغییر خواهد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001792643.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘Have you heard from Ann?’ ‘No, not a word.’","translation":"«از آن شنیده‌ای؟» «نه، یک کلمه نیست.»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001792644.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was still no word from John.","translation":"هنوز از جان خبری نبود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001792645.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s a very small town and if you do something bad, word gets around.","translation":"این یک شهر بسیار کوچک است و اگر کار بدی انجام دهید، اخبار به گوش می رسد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000496394.mp3"},{"sentence":"The word is that the two companies are planning a merger.","translation":"حرف این است که این دو شرکت در حال برنامه ریزی برای ادغام هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000496398.mp3"},{"sentence":"Health officials are encouraging people to spread the word about the benefits of exercise.","translation":"مقامات بهداشتی مردم را تشویق می کنند تا در مورد فواید ورزش صحبت کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001792649.mp3"},{"sentence":"The mayor sent word he’d be late.","translation":"شهردار خبر داد که دیر خواهد آمد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000496405.mp3"},{"sentence":"Word of mouth (= information you get by someone telling you ) is one of the best ways of getting business.","translation":"تبلیغات شفاهی (= اطلاعاتی که توسط کسی که به شما می گوید دریافت می کنید) یکی از بهترین راه های کسب و کار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001792652.mp3"},{"sentence":"Much of this information is picked up by word of mouth from previous students.","translation":"بسیاری از این اطلاعات به صورت شفاهی از دانش آموزان قبلی دریافت می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001792658.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
